A||||8||Pike||Getrag: What year/What Model?||||1||
Z||000000||Pike||10-07-2001||10:05 PM||||I am now beginning my hunt for a Getrad GT Fiero...Can anyone please tell me what years they were used? Any Identifying markings a novice could look for?<BR>Thanks,<BR>Pike||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-07-2001||10:13 PM||||86 1/2 GT - 88 GT with 5 speed transmission. Or 87-88 2m6 with 5 speed transmission.<P>The 4 cylinder Fieros had Isusu 5 speed transmissions.<P>The 85-86 GT had 4 speed transmissions.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Pheagey||10-07-2001||10:33 PM||||Old Lar to my knowledge the '88 4 cyc. (coups) also had the Getrad trannies.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||10-07-2001||10:46 PM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pheagey:<BR><B>Old Lar to my knowledge the '88 4 cyc. (coups) also had the Getrad trannies.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Nope.  No 4-cyl. Fiero came with the Getrag 5-sp.......only V-6 models did.  <P>Beginning in late '86 all V-6 models (GT & SE) came with the Getrag.  <p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 10-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Pike||10-07-2001||10:54 PM||||Thanks for the info guys...<BR>best regards,<BR>Pike||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gerald||10-07-2001||10:59 PM||||I thought the 86 1/2 GT had a 4 speed. Guess im wrong.||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfiero||10-07-2001||11:07 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Gerald:<BR><B>I thought the 86 1/2 GT had a 4 speed. Guess im wrong.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>This debate gets rehashed every so often.....the '86 GT was introduced late in the production year.  I think it was June.  The first ones had the 4-sp. Muncie, but the last 2500 or so got the Getrag.<P>Some people like to call the Getrag equipped GT's 86 1/2, while others suggest the "1/2" label is due to it being released late in the year (most cars are first produced in Sept of the previous year).  <P>So an '86 1/2 GT could conceiveably have a 4 or 5-speed tranny.....it depends on which school of thought you belong to.<P>I personally call all '86 GT's '86 GT's......I HATE the "1/2" monikers.....it just confuses the issue.<BR> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000007||GarethWright||10-08-2001||04:17 AM||||Will the Isuzu 5-spd from a 4-cyl fit a v6?  Will it take the power?||||reg||1
Z||000008||LS1swap||10-09-2001||08:41 PM||||"Will the Isuzu 5-spd from a 4-cyl fit a v6? Will it take the power?"<P>Yes and yes but i do like the getrag better||||reg||1
